Why "Operating System" Triggers Legal Caution
Risk Category	Issue
Heavy Claim	OS implies kernel control, hardware management, system calls, memory/scheduling/drivers
Misrepresentation	Investor confusion, false advertising, regulatory disclosure issues
Liability Difference	OS = kernel ownership, hardware responsibility, root-level security, compliance exposure
Platform = runs on Linux, uses K8s, orchestration + governance layer, no kernel replacement	
Trademark Sensitivity	Big companies (Microsoft, Apple, Linux Foundation) protect system-layer terminology
Patent Review	OS claim invites scrutiny, patent review, competitive analysis, kernel-comparison audits
Security/Compliance	OS expectation = kernel-level CVE response, hardware driver responsibility, secure boot, memory isolation
Platform = govern behavior only; Linux handles kernel isolation; K8s handles orchestration	
Smart Framing Strategy

    ✅ "MeowTada is a Cloud Operating Environment built on Linux and Kubernetes."

